/target
/fixtures/*
# The measurement record is tracked; the raw prover traces are not. With RUST_LOG on,
# a full-scale run emits ~135k span lines — 261 MB for 33 lines of signal — so each run
# is distilled to a *.summary.log and the trace stays local.
!/fixtures/probe-*.log
!/fixtures/smoke-*.log
!/fixtures/s2-*.log
!/fixtures/s3-*.log
!/fixtures/*.summary.log
# The switch list the CPU arm of every GPU comparison was taken under: it is cited by
# knowledge/gpu-proving.md and is the difference between a reproducible pair and a claim.
!/fixtures/cpu-arm-switches.txt
# The full-soundness on-chain fixture is the acceptance evidence for the wrapped proof — the
# artefact the gas figures are measured on — and at ~1.2 KB there is no reason for it to live
# only on one machine. Only the 219-response fixture is tracked: it is the one the Foundry
# suite reads, and a fixture from a probe at another count would outlive the keys it was
# made under without anything reading it to notice. It is safe to track only because the
# Foundry suite refuses a fixture it should not accept (journal version, fingerprint, verifying key,
# single-byte version, proof format, and the 219-response count), each guard validated by
# staging a corrupted fixture; before those existed, a stale tracked fixture would have
# been worse than none.
verifier/fixtures/*
!verifier/fixtures/lift-219.onchain.json
verifier/out
verifier/cache
